# examples/input/01_actions, played: named actions from the keyboard, the
# gamepad and the mouse; the pause menu that takes them all; and a click on
# its Resume button that does not also fire. See tests/e2e/script.h.

# --- the happy path: move, jump, fire ---------------------------------------

# 200 pixels a second: D for half a second is 100 to the right, and the
# d-pad's down -- the same "move_down" action, out of the box -- 100 down.
1 press KEY_D
31 release KEY_D
31 press GAMEPAD_BUTTON_LEFT_FACE_DOWN
61 release GAMEPAD_BUTTON_LEFT_FACE_DOWN

# "jump" is Space and the gamepad's A; "fire" is the left mouse button. The
# HUD says the pointer is down in the frame it is.
62 tap KEY_SPACE
64 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_RIGHT_FACE_DOWN
66 click 600 400
66 shot fire
66 expect scene GameScene

# --- the failure path: what does nothing ------------------------------------

# F is bound to nothing; Q is "aim_left", which the game defines and never
# reads. Neither does anything.
68 tap KEY_F
70 tap KEY_Q

# Escape is "pause": the pause menu goes on top, and takes the input.
72 tap KEY_ESCAPE
72 expect scene PauseScene

# Under it the game hears nothing: D moves nothing, and a click on the veil
# fires nothing. (Space would: it is "jump" to the game, and it presses the
# focused Resume button to the menu -- the UI's Enter.)
74 press KEY_D
88 release KEY_D
89 click 600 400
89 expect scene PauseScene
100 shot paused

# Resume, with the mouse: the click that presses it is no shot in the game.
101 click 400 245
101 expect scene PauseScene
102 expect scene GameScene
113 shot resumed
113 end
